  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm not too sure if this is something I'm doing wrong or just a part of the game, but in desktop mode when you look up or down, your avatar's head only goes about 45 degrees in both directions and, configuring the muscle settings in unity does not seem to affect this at all. This issue only affects desktop, in VR your head can tilt all the way up or down. If this is a 'feature' in the game, why does this happen and can you remove this dumb thing? It makes it kinda hard to make head-following objects for desktop users go past this 45 degrees of rotation.",
